Z||000016||Tigger||04-10-2001||05:08 PM||||I almost forgot, you can make a sit-n-spin for your kids.<P>Here's what you do.  Take some heavy plywood and cut out a 2 ft circle.  Drill the 5x100mm pattern in the center and also drill a clearance hole in the center so it clears the bearing housing and bolt it to the rotor.  Now, take the rotor w/some worn bearings and bolt it to a junk spindle.  Next, cut out a 6" dia. plate and weld it on top of a 1" dia. tube that's about 6-7" long.  Weld that to the end of the spindle.<P>Loads of fun and you'll be so proud  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000017||88formula||04-10-2001||08:15 PM||||Bring them to a scrap metal place and see what you get for them. Maybe you might get $.50.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
